IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dda-core`
IMPORT `dda-seat`
IMPORT `dda-seat-defendant`

-- Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) -- cases for the defendant's seat (dda-seat-defendant.l4), every exported question, with
-- mirror cases: the same facts asked from the claimant's seat (dda-seat.l4) must give the same answer. Every expected
-- value was worked by hand from the deposited text of the Act and the Dust Diseases Regulations 2021, never copied from
-- the encoding's output.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the defendant`

`contrib yes` MEANS `yes: proceedings for contribution between tortfeasors liable for the dust disease damage may be brought before SAET and dealt with by the South Australian Employment Court (s 4A(3))`
`contrib none` MEANS `not covered: s 4A(3) speaks only of contribution between tortfeasors each liable for damages for a dust disease or a death from one`

`d knew yes` MEANS `yes: the person who carried on the process is presumed to have known at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could result in a dust disease, unless the contrary is proved (s 8(2))`
`d knew rebutted` MEANS `no: the contrary has been proved, so the s 8(2) presumption gives way (s 8(2))`
`d knew not prescribed` MEANS `no: the process is not a prescribed industrial or commercial process at that time (s 8(2), reg 4 and Sch 1)`

`d ex yes` MEANS `yes: the court should award exemplary damages against this defendant (s 9(2))`
`d ex no a` MEANS `no: s 9(2) does not direct an award of exemplary damages on these facts, because it is not shown that the defendant knew of the risk of exposure or carried on a Schedule 2 process that resulted in the exposure (s 9(2)(a)); the general law of exemplary damages is untouched`
`d ex no b` MEANS `no: s 9(2) does not direct an award of exemplary damages on these facts, because it is not shown that the defendant knew at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could result in a dust disease (s 9(2)(b)); the general law of exemplary damages is untouched`

`d sell` MEANS `sale or other supply of asbestos products by someone other than their manufacturer`
`d make` MEANS `manufacture of asbestos products`

§§ `s 4A(3): contribution in SAET`

#ASSERT `Can I claim contribution in SAET` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `contrib yes`
#ASSERT `Can I claim contribution in SAET` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `contrib none`
#ASSERT `Can I claim contribution in SAET` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `contrib none`

§§ `s 8(2): presumed knowledge, with mirrors`

-- A retailer of asbestos products (items 7(a), 7(b)): 21 persons from 1 January 1960, otherwise from 1 July 1971.
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 21 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `d knew yes`
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `d knew not prescribed`
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 7 1971) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `d knew yes`
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 7 1971) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `d knew rebutted`
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 21 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 21 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 1960) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 7 1971) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` `d sell` 20 FALSE (`the date` 1 7 1971) TRUE TRUE

§§ `s 9(2): exemplary damages, with mirrors`

#ASSERT `Should exemplary damages be awarded against me` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d make` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d ex yes`
#ASSERT `Should exemplary damages be awarded against me` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d make` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `d ex no b`
#ASSERT `Should exemplary damages be awarded against me` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d sell` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d ex no a`
#ASSERT `Should exemplary damages be awarded against me` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d make` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d make` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Should exemplary damages be awarded against me` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d make` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d make` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Should exemplary damages be awarded against me` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d sell` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `d sell` 40 FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1965) TRUE FALSE FALSE

§§ `s 11(3): the insurer's cap, with mirrors`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be made to pay as the insurer` 1200000 1000000 EQUALS 1000000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be made to pay as the insurer` 1000001 1000000 EQUALS 1000000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be made to pay as the insurer` 999999 1000000 EQUALS 999999
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be made to pay as the insurer` 1000001 1000000 EQUALS `How much can I recover from the insurer` 1000001 1000000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be made to pay as the insurer` 999999 1000000 EQUALS `How much can I recover from the insurer` 999999 1000000
